# Binary file types — never run line-ending conversion or text diff on these.
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows checkouts emits noisy warnings
# about LF/CRLF on the doc PDFs and could in theory corrupt them.
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary

# Forward-compat fixture vault — byte-identity across platforms is the whole
# point. The meta-test (recover/tests/fixture-vault.test.ts) verifies SHA-256
# of every file against a manifest. Without `-text`, Git's core.autocrlf=true
# on Windows checkouts would expand LF → CRLF, breaking the byte-identity
# guarantee.
recover/fixtures/**/*.json -text
recover/fixtures/manifest.json -text
